<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 4.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 4.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's National Coffee Growers' Federation cut the country's internal coffee price by 4.3 percent Friday, setting it at 317,000 pesos per 125-kg load, a federation spokesman said.</p>
<p>The cut in the price paid to growers was the ninth since Jan. 31, when a sliding scale formula was introduced to adjust it on a weekly basis.</p>
<p>The federation spokesman said the new price was based on an average low trading price of $190.00 per pound for Colombian coffee in New York.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
